# Defra design and patterns

- Check the GOV.UK Design System first. If it doesn't cover the need, check Defra's own components and patterns before building anything bespoke: <https://digital.defra.gov.uk/design/components-and-patterns>
- Contact DesignOps before building a bespoke component or pattern: **DesignOps@defra.gov.uk**
- Follow Defra branding guidance: <https://digital.defra.gov.uk/design/branding>
- Internal services and case-management tools must be visually and functionally consistent across Defra, not just within this service.
- `DEFRA/pattern-library` on GitHub is archived (since 2019) — do not use it as a source.
- Prototyping is mandatory for Defra service assessments: <https://digital.defra.gov.uk/design/prototyping>. When creating a new version, record what changed and which research finding or decision drove it — that's the evidence an assessment panel will ask to see.
